# This is a file of tests for the GMOS sequencer in a suitable format to be read
# by the tcsTests.tk procedure.
# 
# This particular file is aimed at checking the input ranges to the commands
# that control the tracking of the detector translation assembly 
#
# Comments are introduced by a # in the first column
# Blank lines can be left if required.
# The currently allowed keywords are (case is immaterial)
#
#  Test   <testId>
#  Command <commandName>
#  Field   <CAD field> <value>
#  Response Accept | Reject
#  Timeout <msecs>
#  OnError Continue | Abort
#  Log     <recordName>
#  Directive Start | Preset

# This first part before the first Test keyword can be used to setup 
# global values for Response, TimeOut and OnError. These global values
# can be over ridden within specific tests

Response Reject
TimeOut  30000
OnError  Continue

Help
Help This test file checks the trapping of invalid input to the dtaTrack
Help
Help The first tests check for null input. If the commands in question have
Help been run at any time after booting and prior to running these tests then
Help there will already be input on the CAD fields and so these null tests
Help will fail. To validate the trapping of null input you will have to
Help reboot the GMOS sequencer and start these tests again.
Help
Help Press continue when ready
Help

# Tests start here. Each test must start with the Test keyword, end with
# a Directive keyword and have at least one Command keyword. Any Field
# keywords are assumed to apply to the last command

Test UT01010
Summary Check rejection of null input to tracking mode 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  DIR MARK   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01020
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to tracking mode 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  XXXXX   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01030
Summary Check rejection of invalid X offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  xxxx 
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01040
Summary Check rejection of out of range X offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B -20.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01050
Summary Check rejection of too large an X offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  2000.0 
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01060
Summary Check rejection of invalid Y offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0 
  Field  C  xxxxx
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01070
Summary Check rejection of out of range Y offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0 
  Field  C  -20.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01080
Summary Check rejection of too large an Y offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0
  Field  C  200.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01090
Summary Check rejection of invalid Z offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0 
  Field  C  0.0 
  Field  D  xxxxx
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01100
Summary Check rejection of out of range Z offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0 
  Field  C  0.0 
  Field  D  -20.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT01110
Summary Check rejection of too large an Z offset 

 Command dtaTrack 
  Field  A  MOVE   
  Field  B  0.0
  Field  C  0.0
  Field  D  20000.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start
 
# Test UT01120
# Summary Check that rejection by Components Controller is reported correctly
# NO TEST AVAILABLE
#

